== saves.py: build a disk, read every save back
ok   build of 601 entries stays near its cluster count (under 16 MiB)
ok   a disk with one small save is under 2 MiB
ok   verify AAAA0001: every file byte for byte
ok   pull AAAA0001 gives the same save id
ok   pull AAAA0001 keeps the raw FATX times
ok   verify BBBB0002: every file byte for byte
ok   pull BBBB0002 gives the same save id
ok   pull BBBB0002 keeps the raw FATX times
ok   verify CCCC0003: every file byte for byte
ok   pull CCCC0003 gives the same save id
ok   pull CCCC0003 keeps the raw FATX times
ok   list sees exactly the three titles
ok   list counts the 300 save dirs of the chained directory
== saves.py: the checks can fail
ok   verify refuses a save whose content differs from the image's
ok   load_save refuses a file that no longer matches save.json
== saves.py: the qcow2 is laid out as qemu-img lays one out
ok   header: qcow2 v3, 64 KiB clusters, 8 GiB, refcount order 4
ok   header: refcount table at 0x10000, L1 at 0x30000, 16 L1 entries
ok   every host cluster has refcount 1, and no other cluster has one
ok   every L1/L2 entry is COPIED and points inside the file
